From 1223324246d83270faf24a8862ad6fb1244ca950 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebastian Droege <sebastian@centricular.com>
Date: Thu, 12 May 2022 17:11:38 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] qtdemux: Don't use tfdt for parsing subsequent trun boxes

The timestamp in the tfdt refers to the first trun box and if there are
multiple trun boxes then the distance between the first timestamps will
grow.

At some point this distance reaches a threshold and triggers the
resetting of the first sample's timestamp of this trun box to be reset
to the tfdt.

This threshold is implemented for files where there is a jump in the
timeline between fragments and where this can be detected via a jump
between the end timestamp of the previous fragment and the tfdt of the
next. This behaviour is preserved.

Backport of upstream commit 1223324246d83270faf24a8862ad6fb1244ca950
(merged for 1.22, MR !2409) onto gst-plugins-good 1.18.5.

Symptom without this patch: fMP4 segments that carry more than one trun
box per traf lose the samples of every trun after the first, because those
samples are assigned the same start timestamp as the first trun and
therefore overlap it. Under MSE the overlapping frames replace the
existing ones, leaving a hole at the end of every fragment, which stops
readyState from ever reaching HAVE_ENOUGH_DATA so playback never starts.

Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/gstreamer/gstreamer/-/merge_requests/2409>

Upstream-Status: Backport [1223324246d83270faf24a8862ad6fb1244ca950]
---
 gst/isomp4/qtdemux.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/gst/isomp4/qtdemux.c
+++ b/gst/isomp4/qtdemux.c
@@ -4051,6 +4051,8 @@ qtdemux_parse_moof (GstQTDemux * qtdemux, const guint8 * buffer, guint length,
       /* iterate all siblings */
       trun_node = qtdemux_tree_get_sibling_by_type_full (trun_node, FOURCC_trun,
           &trun_data);
+      /* don't use tfdt for subsequent trun as it only refers to the first */
+      tfdt_node = NULL;
     }
 
     uuid_node = qtdemux_tree_get_child_by_type (traf_node, FOURCC_uuid);
